        "surveyType": "Standard Survey",
        "narrative": "<p>Lake trout were apparently abundant but small in Bat Lake in 2004.  Lake trout (Gillis Lake strain) were introduced in this lake in 1982, and since 1991 the population has been self-sustained.  Lake trout growth was very slow - six-year-old fish were just 11.5 to 17.8 inches long when collected in July 2004.  Slow growth was due to the relatively high number of lake trout present, and the limited forage available for those fish.  White sucker were the only other fish taken in the 2004 survey.  They weren't abundant, and were too large to have been taken by lake trout.</p>",
